# Öpik's b-Plane Parametric Phase Sweep for (99942) Apophis (2029 Encounter)

[![License: MIT](https://shields.io)](https://opensource.org)
[![Preprint DOI](https://shields.io)](https://doi.org)

## Overview
High-precision numerical simulation framework developed in Python to map the non-linear arrival phase sensitivity of near-Earth asteroid **(99942) Apophis** on Öpik's *b*-plane during its April 13, 2029 terrestrial flyby. This repository accompanies the manuscript submitted to *The Planetary Science Journal* (Manuscript ID: `AAS83688`).

## Key Features & Methodology
* **Integrator:** Implicit 15th-order Gauss–Radau adaptive solver (`IAS15`, truncation tolerance $\epsilon = 10^{-12}$) implemented within the `REBOUND` ecosystem.
* **Ephemerides:** Initialized with live geocentric and heliocentric state vectors retrieved via `Astroquery` from NASA JPL Horizons.
* **Parametric Sweep:** Evaluates 25 arrival phase offsets ($\Delta t \in [-60, +60]$ minutes in 5-minute steps), identifying the direct terrestrial impact threshold ($r_p = 6,221.45\text{ km}$ at $\Delta t = -30\text{ min}$) and computing the equivalent 5-year lead-time along-track kinetic deflection impulse ($\Delta v = 116.739\text{ mm/s}$).

## Installation & Execution
```bash
pip install rebound astroquery numpy matplotlib
python apophis_psj_parametric_sweep.py
```

